more important than quantity.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:07.200
- That's big. Tell us about that.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.780
- And let me finish and say,

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:12.550
but I actually think it's
both quality and quantity.

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:13.400
But if you had to pick one,

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.640
I think quality is now the dominant thing.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:17.530
Now, that's kind of a very confusing thing

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:20.110
that can intimidate people
because they think, okay, wait,

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:22.110
I gotta get a $4,000 red camera

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:23.240
and I gotta get custom lighting.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:24.073
It's not that.

00:01:24.073 --> 00:01:27.130
It's the content value,
not the production value.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:29.020
It might be something shot on a phone.

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:31.280
It doesn't even mean
that it's super planned.

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:33.900
But what it means is that quality matters.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.730
And I think that what we saw in the past

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:39.620
was sometimes a pressure to
just go like live every day,

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:41.310
just get like a lot of
content and be there.

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:45.440
But that content had no value
a week later or a month later,

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:48.120
or to just try to put out as
many pieces of content a day.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.260
And, of course, Gary V. is
talking about like published 50,

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:51.840
100 pieces of content a day.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.950
And that's the quantity
piece that does matter.

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:58.540
But what I'm talking about
is I think the trend is

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:03.320
that quality is what rises
to the top on any platform.

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:07.060
That in some cases with
organic reach going down,

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:10.220
you might only get a few chances
to get in front of people.

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:11.680
So here's the question to ask,

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:13.830
what experience are they
having with your brand

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:15.670
when you get that chance.

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:17.890
When they get to meet you
and they give you a shot,

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:19.460
they see your video in their feed,

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:21.030
they see that YouTube video,

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:22.560
you even rank for a search term.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:25.730
And when you first optimize a
video, it shows up on YouTube

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:27.590
and they might let you rank for awhile

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:29.010
and they're going to see
what people think about it.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:32.030
And when people watch that
video, what is their experience?

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:34.250
And I think because we now have helped

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:36.100
even over like almost 4,000 people in

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:39.010
our Video Ranking Academy community,

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:41.670
I've noticed that sometimes
people just feel this pressure

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:43.370
and they feel like it's
like a badge of honor.

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:45.200
I upload seven days a week

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.160
and I almost feel like
maybe you should upload

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:48.360
only one day a week,

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.500
but take all the energy you
are putting into the seven

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:52.700
into one to make it higher quality.

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:54.550
The last analogy when I think of quality

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:56.480
is the difference between writing a book

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.280
and writing a tweet.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:02:59.880
A lot of people feel the pressure

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:02.470
to post on Instagram
every day, write a tweet,

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:04.210
post on Twitter 10 times a day.

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:05.380
But someone who sits down,

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:07.210
and there's a great book
about this called Deep Work

00:03:07.210 --> 00:03:08.980
by Cal Newport, who's known for

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:11.130
not really being on
social media that much,

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:12.970
but when he puts out a blog post,

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:15.160
very rarely or when he puts out a book,

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:17.460
it is a bestseller and it impacts

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:19.970
and it lives on for weeks,
months, and years to come.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:21.870
Now, I'm not saying every
YouTube video is a book.

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:25.150
I'm saying that's the mindset,
is leaning more on quality

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:26.060
because what we've learned

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:28.120
with YouTube being a search
engine ranking videos

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:30.910
that when we take longer
to make something better

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:33.900
that we can reap the rewards
from that piece of content

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.340
for weeks, months, and years to come.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:37.240
When we rush something, we might get

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:38.900
some quick action that day,

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:40.630
but we have to wake up the next day.

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:43.470
It's like fast fashion versus
something high quality.

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:45.640
It's like investing in
something you wash twice

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:46.910
and it falls apart versus something

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:49.840
you can hand down to your
kids for generations.

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:53.270
Quality over quantity in 2020

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:54.950
- I love how you said
that at the beginning too.

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:57.090
It doesn't necessarily
mean the production value,

00:03:57.090 --> 00:04:00.600
so I can still produce
content with my smartphone,

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:02.730
but it's the quality of the content.

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:04.670
It's what you're putting out there.

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:06.160
And it's leveling up, obviously,

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:08.881
you don't wanna just
everything to be raw and real.

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:11.820
It should definitely
have value wrapped in it.

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:12.910
But I love that you said,

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:15.370
it's not necessarily
about leveling up the tech

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:17.830
because that's not necessarily
what's gonna change it.

00:04:17.830 --> 00:04:20.330
It really is about the
content and the value

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:21.320
that you're exchanging

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.090
- The substance, and you're
a great example of this.

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:26.228
On your homeschool channel,
you think about the substance

00:04:26.228 --> 00:04:28.760
and in other cases, when
it comes to homeschool,

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:30.390
how many books have you read on the topic?

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:32.700
- Almost everyone out, maybe 50 bucks.

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:34.950
- So I think a lot of people

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:37.750
when it comes to mastering
their subject matter,

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:40.340
they have read no books about this subject

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:41.630
or they've read one and they have

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:43.400
a surface level understanding.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:45.350
When you've read 50 versus reading one,

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:48.350
your depth of knowledge
and even your comparison

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:51.580
of the different ideas is
deeper, that's substance.

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:54.060
So if you just shoot
on a webcam with, yes,

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.110
I think you do need it,

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:56.060
and that's what we have at Think Media.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:58.650
So our channel all about
tech, you need some lighting

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:00.270
and maybe a USB microphone,

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:01.930
but this stuff doesn't
have to break the bank.

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:04.390
For like $100, you could
get a webcam, a USB mic

00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:05.410
and you're good to go.

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:07.980
But the substance of what you're teaching,

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:11.290
so taking more time on the
content that you're creating

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:12.890
and then speed also matters as well.

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:14.500
And here's maybe the best way to put this.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.170
We are applying these trends.

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:17.820
These are the trends we're living.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:21.190
I have felt, we have felt
when it comes to Think Media,

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:23.930
video influencers, a
decline in organic reach

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:26.440
by just doing the same things
we've been doing in the past,

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:29.570
same old thumbnails,
kind of same old content,

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:31.130
same old videos over and over.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.400
That's why we're launching
the Think Marketing Show.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:35.620
We're trying to do new
things, do different things,

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:37.530
starting videos in different ways.

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:40.480
Really actually think about
mastering an organization

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:41.890
of what we're putting together.

00:05:41.890 --> 00:05:44.750
We realize we need to level up,

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:45.583
and that's what I'm saying.

00:05:45.583 --> 00:05:48.650
In 2020 and beyond, you have
to invest in your skills.

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:50.400
Take your quality to another level.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:52.600
Don't compare yourself to
anybody on the right or the left,

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:55.240
but just say, how do I take
my quality to a higher level?

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:57.800
Substance as well as
the overall presentation

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:00.380
of the value I'm
delivering to the end user.

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:01.620
- So key, so key.

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:03.740
So number two, what's the second trend

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:06.050
that you're seeing
happening going into 2020

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:08.640
that business owners,
and content creators,

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:11.880
and nonprofit owners, and churches need

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:12.973
to be taking a notice too?

00:06:12.973 --> 00:06:17.580
- Yeah, I think the other big
trend is short form video,

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:19.930
and this shouldn't come
as news to anybody,

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:22.230
but we've seen Instagram stories,

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:24.300
Tik Tok is blowing up,
and that's something

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:25.830
that could be interesting to people.

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:27.930
But stories are also on Facebook.

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:29.360
Stories are also on YouTube.

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:31.380
And if you already have some
YouTube influence, shoot,

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:32.213
I mean that--

00:06:32.213 --> 00:06:33.880
You were just telling me,
like I gotta double down

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:35.640
because we have YouTube influence,

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:36.950
but it's kind of a
feature that you're like,

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:38.460
you forget that it's there.

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:40.750
And I think there's a couple
of things with stories.

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:42.850
Not only is it the fact that

00:06:42.850 --> 00:06:44.690
there's the chance to reach people

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:46.790
and go deeper with your current community,

00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:50.160
but it's actually learning
a new way of communication,

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:51.750
like learning to communicate on stories.

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:54.360
I remember even when
Snapchat was first big

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:56.260
for a little bit wider of an audience,

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:58.350
it's still going for
a certain younger age,

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:02.220
but now it's mainly Instagram
stories and Facebook stories,

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:04.910
that at first it was almost like

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:07.070
it took another part of my brain

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:08.530
and it sort of stressed me out,

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:11.010
and I only was thinking
in long form YouTube,

00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:13.540
and I didn't think I had
the bandwidth to do it.

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:15.160
And I dunno, let us know in the comments

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:16.110
if you've ever felt that way.

00:07:16.110 --> 00:07:17.770
Like, I gotta learn something new

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:19.630
because that is how it feels at first.

00:07:19.630 --> 00:07:21.550
But just like learning to ride a bike

00:07:21.550 --> 00:07:23.120
or just like learning a new skill set.

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:24.380
Like, at one point, you had to learn

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:26.480
how to use Microsoft Word
or turn the computer on

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:27.640
or how to use Excel,

00:07:27.640 --> 00:07:29.350
but then it just became a core competency

00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:30.730
that you do without thinking.

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:32.210
It almost like a habit.

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:35.070
That short form communication

00:07:35.070 --> 00:07:36.820
is something that we need to learn.

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:38.267
Quick hits of information,

00:07:38.267 --> 00:07:41.310
communicating in short sound bites

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:43.531
and being able to stitch
together different pieces

00:07:43.531 --> 00:07:45.680
of communication we found.

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:48.300
I mean, our business has
scaled and grown from

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.480
how I use Instagram stories,

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:54.210
how Think Media as a team
repurposes some of those things

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:56.440
turns them into video ads
or turns them into posts

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:57.850
on other platforms.

00:07:57.850 --> 00:08:00.210
We're using stories in
a lot of creative ways.

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:03.320
So I think short form video,
in general, is a major trend

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:04.860
that people need to be paying attention to

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:05.693
and leaning in on.

00:08:05.693 --> 00:08:06.570
I mean, how do you feel about it?

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:09.130
- Yeah, I think what I love
about short form is that

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:11.070
it can be real and raw and in the moment.

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:13.920
I know we've talked about
it on Think Media before,

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:16.620
but your vlog, people
say, "Sean, we wanna see

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:17.453
a vlog from you."

00:08:17.453 --> 00:08:20.270
And you say, "I got that.
It's over on Instagram.

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:22.630
You can go follow you on Instagram.

00:08:22.630 --> 00:08:24.120
And you see the Rise &amp; Grind show.

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:26.880
That is your daily vlog
of how you're showing

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:28.880
the behind the scenes of what's happening.

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:30.530
And followers love that.

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:33.400
They really love being able
to be a part of your world

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:34.410
and they're getting to know you.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:35.610
They're getting to know your wife,

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:36.910
they're getting to know your dogs,

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:38.750
they're getting to know
your favorite green juice,

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:41.243
they're starting to find
these similarities with you.

00:08:41.243 --> 00:08:44.130
What I love about it is, for me,

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:46.250
I was scared to get on camera.

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:48.630
It was something that
wasn't natural to me.

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:53.580
And so, I used it because
it goes away on Snapchat

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:56.050
or before, I'm sorry,
on Instagram stories.

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:57.980
You can use it and it goes away.

00:08:57.980 --> 00:08:59.990
So if you mess up, that's fine.

00:08:59.990 --> 00:09:03.140
It's just a short form piece of content.

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:05.880
But it is such a great way
of being able to tell a story

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:07.220
and be able to communicate.

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:09.310
And I think if business
owners, or churches,

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:11.890
or nonprofits grasp this concept

00:09:11.890 --> 00:09:14.450
and can communicate in small pieces,

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:17.730
they can earn trust in
a very small way first

00:09:17.730 --> 00:09:19.860
then leading them into longer form.

00:09:19.860 --> 00:09:23.170
So when you're shouting out a
video that's over on YouTube,

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:25.440
you're giving value in 15 seconds,

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:29.380
but leading them to maybe a
20-minute or 30-minute video,

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:30.640
they've gained that trust with you.

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:33.020
And so, they will go and
make that connection.

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:35.630
So it's a really great tool to be using

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:37.080
for yourself as a communicator,

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:39.670
but also to be able to build
trust with your audience.

